{
  "document": "trace2skill-prompts",
  "policyVersion": "trace2skill-jtlt-v1",
  "prompts": [
    {
      "id": "draft",
      "role": "draft",
      "policyVersion": "trace2skill-jtlt-v1",
      "sourceDigest": "9b16936c63fb1bcab28fcdb09eea482cc7ba656c9166147ab8d0af4f8de9848d",
      "pack": {
        "meta": {
          "id": "draft",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "role": "draft"
        },
        "system": {
          "content": "You write the first version of a skill directory for one bounded domain.\n\nReply with a root page `SKILL.md` and, if it helps, files under\n`references/`. Write only what is true of the DOMAIN: how its inputs are\nread, what shape an answer takes, which mistakes are easy to make. You have\nseen no example of the work and must not invent one — no sample question,\nno sample answer, no identifier. Every link you write must reach a file you\nalso return."
        },
        "user": {
          "content": "{{scope}}"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "scope": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "render": "text"
        }
      },
      "variableSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "scope": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "files"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "files": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 16,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "path",
                "content"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "path": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "maxLength": 512
                },
                "content": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "userStylesheet": {
        "$jtlt": "0.1",
        "output": "text",
        "rules": [
          {
            "match": "$",
            "body": [
              "$.variables.scope"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "revision": "db2c9ad02afd614f89df3ab4751d7f9876b37e62b27ce5d7241d02c613da307b"
    },
    {
      "id": "executor",
      "role": "executor",
      "policyVersion": "trace2skill-jtlt-v1",
      "sourceDigest": "c3208e1be8e58bf34eaecc0c5414773b9f95f190b4d7ada1199a4602b93d3da5",
      "pack": {
        "meta": {
          "id": "executor",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "role": "executor"
        },
        "system": {
          "content": "You answer exactly one question about the files named in the task.\n\nRead the files you need with the tools you were given, then reply with the\nbare answer and nothing else — no sentence, no units, no restatement of the\nquestion. If a skill directory is present below, it is the authority on how\nthis domain is read and how an answer is written."
        },
        "user": {
          "content": "{{task}}{{#if inputs}}\n\nFiles named by this task:\n{{inputs}}{{/if}}"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "task": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "render": "text"
        },
        "inputs": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 0
          },
          "render": "text"
        }
      },
      "variableSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "task": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "inputs": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 0
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "task"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": true,
      "userStylesheet": {
        "$jtlt": "0.1",
        "output": "text",
        "rules": [
          {
            "match": "$",
            "body": [
              "$.variables.task",
              {
                "$apply": [
                  "$",
                  "condition-1"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "mode": "condition-1",
            "priority": 1,
            "match": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "present"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "present": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "required": [
                      "inputs"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "inputs": {
                        "const": true
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "body": [
              "\n\nFiles named by this task:\n",
              "$.variables.inputs"
            ]
          },
          {
            "mode": "condition-1",
            "body": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "revision": "bb23faa1f675d616b620405938e8404a643c3807c5f4c1a9febb9ddf3d0374a9"
    },
    {
      "id": "success-analyst",
      "role": "success-analyst",
      "policyVersion": "trace2skill-jtlt-v1",
      "sourceDigest": "a9ea1d05e5024ee10a6787147a932d50dd3c0f4f6ed43a5e5b4e0a91a8f68bad",
      "pack": {
        "meta": {
          "id": "success-analyst",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "role": "success-analyst"
        },
        "system": {
          "content": "You read ONE successful trajectory and say what a skill directory should\nrecord so the next attempt at this KIND of task goes the same way.\n\nName every reusable behaviour you can support from the steps, and cite the\nstep indexes each one is read from. Then either propose one directory patch\nthat writes those behaviours down, or return a null patch when the directory\nalready says everything this trajectory used. Write guidance about the\ndomain, never about this instance: no task identifier, no input path, no\nanswer, no copied span from the transcript."
        },
        "user": {
          "content": "{{evidence}}"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "evidence": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "render": "text"
        }
      },
      "variableSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "evidence": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "evidence"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "$id": "https://tangleai.dev/schemas/trace2skill/successAnalysis",
        "description": "What one successful trajectory taught, in a single pass. The patterns cite the steps they were read from, so a claim with no step behind it is visible; a null patch says the directory already covers this trajectory.",
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "patterns": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 8,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "behavior": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "evidenceStepIndexes": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/count"
                  }
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "behavior",
                "evidenceStepIndexes"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "patch": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/authoredPatch"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ]
          },
          "reasoning": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "patterns",
          "patch",
          "reasoning"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$defs": {
          "count": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0
          },
          "authoredPatch": {
            "description": "A directory patch as a role writes it: the edits and the reason for them. Identity, run, frozen base hash, provenance and support are sealed by the dispatcher from what it already knows, so nothing here asks a model for a receipt it cannot compute.",
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "reasoning": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "operations": {
                "type": "array",
                "minItems": 1,
                "maxItems": 16,
                "items": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/patchOperation"
                }
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "reasoning",
              "operations"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "patchOperation": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/createFileOperation"
              },
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/insertOperation"
              },
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/sectionOperation"
              }
            ]
          },
          "createFileOperation": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "op": {
                "const": "create_file"
              },
              "path": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/skillPath"
              },
              "group": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "op",
              "path",
              "group",
              "content"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "skillPath": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 512,
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9._][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*$"
          },
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "insertOperation": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "op": {
                "enum": [
                  "insert_before",
                  "insert_after"
                ]
              },
              "path": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/skillPath"
              },
              "group": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
              },
              "anchor": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "op",
              "path",
              "group",
              "anchor",
              "content"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "sectionOperation": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "op": {
                "enum": [
                  "replace_section",
                  "delete_section"
                ]
              },
              "path": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/skillPath"
              },
              "group": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
              },
              "from": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1
              },
              "to": {
                "type": [
                  "string",
                  "null"
                ]
              },
              "content": {
                "type": [
                  "string",
                  "null"
                ]
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "op",
              "path",
              "group",
              "from",
              "to",
              "content"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        }
      },
      "userStylesheet": {
        "$jtlt": "0.1",
        "output": "text",
        "rules": [
          {
            "match": "$",
            "body": [
              "$.variables.evidence"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "revision": "5e497f6900bb936fc37ebbc6507bf65d29eee53ad82d232c54e09044dab23e88"
    },
    {
      "id": "error-analyst",
      "role": "error-analyst",
      "policyVersion": "trace2skill-jtlt-v1",
      "sourceDigest": "c1a6d17cfb4800e9bfb8db70273151ac6196db764e12c3acd580f0cfc51f3d14",
      "pack": {
        "meta": {
          "id": "error-analyst",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "role": "error-analyst"
        },
        "system": {
          "content": "You diagnose ONE failed trajectory and may propose a directory patch only\nafter you have proved a repair.\n\nRead the trace, read the registered answer, then rewrite the answer in the\noverlay and run `evaluate`. Propose only once `evaluate` has passed over\nyour rewrite: the proposal must cite the step indexes that failed, the\nmismatch, the repair you made, the evaluation attempt that passed and why\nthe guidance generalizes. Write guidance about the domain, never about this\ninstance: no task identifier, no input path, no answer, no copied span.\nIf you cannot find a repair the evaluator accepts, stop without proposing."
        },
        "user": {
          "content": "{{evidence}}"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "evidence": {
          "schema": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "render": "text"
        }
      },
      "variableSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "evidence": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "evidence"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
